# Evidence rules

Before editing, record:
- origin/main SHA;
- current branch;
- current HEAD;
- working-tree state;
- authorized starting SHA;
- active PR number, if any.

Before handoff:
1. Fetch the live remote state.
2. Derive all commits since the authorized starting SHA.
3. Classify each commit:
   - runtime;
   - schema/migration;
   - database tooling;
   - test;
   - CI;
   - documentation;
   - empty retrigger;
   - independent review report.
4. Derive the actual last runtime/test implementation commit from Git history.
5. Distinguish:
   - starting main;
   - runtime/test implementation head;
   - reviewed implementation head;
   - review-report-only commit;
   - documentation finalization head;
   - live PR head.
6. Verify CI head_sha equals the live PR head.
7. Record superseded failed and cancelled CI runs.
8. Never call a branch complete based only on a report.
9. Never put a commit's own unknown future SHA inside that same commit.
10. After any documentation sync commit, obtain CI again if exact-head CI is required.

Required final checks:
- git status --porcelain
- git diff --check
- git rev-parse HEAD
- git rev-parse origin/main
- live PR head
- live CI head_sha